      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T17:23:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about doing this but decided against it because of the mapping from PORT number to Zephyr PORT device ```pdc_data[port]-\u003eport```. I would need to pass both PORT number and pointer to PORT device to the policy API if it were in another file. ``` enforce_pd_chipset_resume_policy_1(int port, struct pdc_port_t *pdc_port) ```. Also since the policy count is low, it seems better to leave them here.",
      "parentUuid": "eeff0210_268466f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1809,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1809,
        "endChar": 29
