      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T19:16:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This file is now nearly 2000 lines long.  I would really like the policy stuff managed in a separate file.\n\nI\u0027m not sure why you would need to pass in both a port number and the `pdc_port` pointer.\n\nYou could manage this using the FOREACH macro:\n\n```\n#define DT_DRV_COMPAT named_usbc_port\n\nresume_policy(const struct device *dev)\n{\n\tstruct pdc_data_t *data \u003d dev-\u003edata;\n\tstruct pdc_port_t *port \u003d \u0026data-\u003eport;\n\t/* ... */\n}\n\n#define PDC_CHIPSET_RESUME_POLICY(inst) \\\n   const struct device *dev \u003d DEVICE_DT_INST_GET(inst); \\\n   resume_policy(dev);\n\n\nstatic void pd_chipset_resume(void) {\n    DT_INST_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY(PDC_CHIPSET_RESUME_POLICY)\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "26f4a8a4_d6e68905",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1809,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1809,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "f302ed6a7ab54d2bcb6407786cd96adfd37adccf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
